<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Joseph Boakai</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. 1944</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Joseph Nyuma Boakai</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Joseph Boakai is a Liberian politician who was vice-president under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ellen-johnson-sirleaf">Ellen Johnson Sirleaf</a> from 2006 to 2018. After losing the 2017 election to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-weah">George Weah</a>, he defeated him in 2023 and became president in January 2024, in a peaceful transfer of power.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/joseph-boakai.jpg" alt="Joseph Boakai" width="320" height="430" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cabinet Public Relations Office of the Cabinet Secretariat · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Joseph_Boakai_in_Yokohama_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
